articipation of their Lebanese counterparts. No written arrest or detention orders are produced at the time of detention.\~
 Second, families experience severe suffering following these state-sanctioned abductions because Lebanese and Syrian authorities do n
ot officially provide information about the detention, fate, or whereabouts of the "disappeared." Third, most victims in cases investigated by Human Rights Watch were tortured while in custody in Syrian detention facilities in Lebanon or while in detentio
n in Syria. In some cases documented by Human Rights Watch, the "disappeared" have been pressured by high-ranking Syrian officers to collaborate with Syrian intelligence in Lebanon.\~\~ }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
